---
id: org.dxos.plugin.heygen
name: HeyGenPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

A **headless** Composer plugin that makes [HeyGen](https://heygen.com) available
as a **video** generation provider for `plugin-studio`. No React/UI surfaces.

## Extensions

| Term   | URI                     |
| ------ | ----------------------- |
| `feat` | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0` |
| `test` | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0` |
| `flow` | `org.dxos.mdl.flow@1.0` |

## Connector

```mdl
feat HeyGenConnector
  desc: >
    Contributes a ConnectorEntry via Capability.contributes(Connector, [entry])
    on SetupConnectors (mirrors plugin-ideogram / plugin-ibkr).
  id: org.dxos.plugin.heygen.connector
  source: heygen.com
  label: HeyGen
  credentialForm:
    schema: HeyGenTokenForm { token: string }   # the API key
    onSubmit: >
      Trim the token; store Obj.make(AccessToken, { source: "heygen.com", token })
      + Obj.make(Connection, { connectorId, accessToken }); return { kind: "complete", … }.
```

## Provider

```mdl
feat HeyGenGenerationService
  desc: >
    Contributes a GenerationService (kind 'video') via
    Capability.contributes(StudioCapabilities.GenerationService, [service]) on Startup.
    Asynchronous: enqueue → awaitResult (poll). Contract from @dxos/plugin-studio/types.
  id: heygen
  kind: video
  contentType: video/mp4
  source: heygen.com
  requestSchema: { avatarId?, voiceId? }        # HeyGen requires both at generate time
  enqueue:
    endpoint: POST https://api.heygen.com/v3/videos   # via edge CORS proxy; header X-Api-Key
    body: { type: 'avatar', avatar_id, voice_id, script: <prompt>, aspect_ratio, resolution, … }
    returns: { jobId: data.video_id }
  awaitResult:
    endpoint: GET https://api.heygen.com/v3/videos/{jobId}   # poll until status 'completed'
    returns: { variants: [{ contentType: 'video/mp4', url, generation: { provider: 'heygen' } }] }
  errors:
    - missing apiKey → MissingApiKey (studio resolves it from the Connector credential first)
    - missing avatar/voice → ProviderFailure
    - non-2xx / status 'failed' / timeout → ProviderFailure
```

## Avatar/voice picker

```mdl
feat HeyGenGenerateForm
  desc: >
    Overrides studio's default schema-driven GenerateForm for kind:'video' with a
    provider-specific picker: `avatarId`/`voiceId` render as SelectFields populated
    from listAvatars()/listVoices(). Contributed as a ReactSurface on the studio
    `GenerateForm` role token (@dxos/plugin-studio/surfaces) with Position.first +
    filter data.kind==='video'. The API key is read from the Connector AccessToken
    (useQuery, source 'heygen.com'). Ported from the former plugin-generator
    GenerationProperties.
```

## Dependencies

- `@dxos/plugin-studio` (workspace:\*) — `/types` (GenerationService contract) + `/surfaces` (GenerateForm role token).
- `@dxos/plugin-connector`, `@dxos/types` (AccessToken), `@dxos/edge-client`
  (CORS proxy), `@dxos/app-framework`, `@dxos/app-toolkit`, `@dxos/echo`,
  `@dxos/invariant`, `@dxos/log`, `@dxos/react-client`, `@dxos/react-ui-form`,
  `react` (peer), `effect`.

## Out of scope (v1)

- Audio generation (HeyGen is video-only).

## QA

Executable flows. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by flow and step number.

```mdl
flow QA-1: Connect a HeyGen key and generate a video
  desc: |
    HeyGen is headless — it contributes a Connector credential form and a GenerationService, but
    owns no UI and no operation of its own. Generation runs entirely through plugin-studio's
    generic `Generate` operation with `provider: "heygen"`; there is no plugin-heygen-local key to
    invoke.
  actors: both
  covers: [HeyGenConnector, HeyGenGenerationService, HeyGenGenerateForm]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - collection: a collection in that space, to create into
    - a valid HeyGen API key
    - no Artifact named "QA Avatar Clip" exists — ABORT rather than reusing one this flow did not create
  test:
    - name: Connect HeyGen
      do: Open Settings -> Connectors -> HeyGen, paste the API key, and submit.
      expect: a Connection + AccessToken pair for source "heygen.com" now exists
      note: |
        NO `invoke` — credential submission goes through the Connector's `onSubmit` UI callback,
        not an operation with a runtime key.
    - name: Create a video Artifact
      do: In the navtree, click + on a collection and choose Studio Artifact, kind Video. Name it "QA Avatar Clip" and enter a script prompt.
      capture: created
      expect: an Artifact of kind "video" named "QA Avatar Clip" exists with the prompt set
      note: |
        NO `invoke` — `Artifact.make()` is wired through `CreateObjectEntry`, the same
        UI-only factory pattern as plugin-game's `createGame` (see that plugin's QA); there is no
        operation key behind object creation itself.
    - name: Generate with HeyGen
      do: In the Artifact's generate panel, pick "HeyGen" as the provider, choose an avatar and voice from the pickers (populated via `listAvatars()`/`listVoices()`), and click Generate.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.studio.generate { artifact: $created.object, provider: "heygen", config: { avatarId: "<picked-avatar-id>", voiceId: "<picked-voice-id>" } }
      capture: generated
      expect: |
        the invoke blocks until HeyGen's job reaches a terminal state (enqueue + awaitResult both
        run inside the operation), and the appended Variant holds a playable video/mp4 URL
      assert: |
        const artifact = await space.db.load($created.object);
        const last = await space.db.load(artifact.variants[artifact.variants.length - 1]);
        return $generated.count === 1 && last.contentType === 'video/mp4' && typeof last.url === 'string' && last.url.length > 0;
      note: Async provider — `enqueue` returns a jobId, `awaitResult` polls `GET /v3/videos/{jobId}` until status 'completed' before the operation returns, so the assert can check the terminal Variant directly.
  after:
    - name: Delete the Artifact
      do: Right-click "QA Avatar Clip" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [$created.object], target: $given.collection }
      expect: the row leaves the navtree and its plank closes if it was open
    - name: Disconnect HeyGen
      do: In Settings -> Connectors -> HeyGen, remove the connection.
      expect: the Connection and its AccessToken are removed
```
